c644fc0\"],\"summary\":\"Playbook (ansible.builtin.user + copy of limits.d/appworker.conf) executed from node2 against node1 via SSH, run reported changed=2, and direct verification on node1 (id, cat limits file, su - appworker ulimit -n/-u) shows account exists with nofile=8192 and nproc=256.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c3b287a4e54a4344\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 242af11e..., uptime since 22:57:39, and confirmed appworker account/limits/ulimit values healthy prior to restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0207d1a1ebd34619\",\"cmd-73820e5006e84579\",\"cmd-311365a25c6740fd\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot was launched in background so the ack returned before disconnect; subsequent poll timed out (node down) then succeeded, showing the node cycled through unavailability.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart boot identity change and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0953ddbff411445e\"],\"summary\":\"New boot_id 595efd98... (changed from 242af11e...) with new boot time 22:59:24; appworker account, limits.d file, live ulimit -n=8192/-u=256, and sshd active all confirmed healthy post-restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (ansible control node) baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c739ec0f94f04d92\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 416c5cf5..., uptime since 22:57:39, and confirmed ansible-core present prior to restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-08d2b782d4d74437\",\"cmd-7f9be6d0215e471b\",\"cmd-3f78a1e0612544f9\",\"cmd-7472d1c70b2b4f56\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot launched in background with ack returned before disconnect; subsequent polls show connection timeout then reset then success, confirming the node cycled down and back up.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart boot identity change and recovered functional state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f5bd01428b3e440b\"],\"summary\":\"New boot_id f1190db0... (changed from 416c5cf5...); re-verified ansible install, live SSH to node1, and a fresh ansible-playbook run against node1 returned changed=0, proving both the control node's tooling and node1's target state (appworker account/limits) survived both restarts intact.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created the appworker account on node1 with session limits of 8192 open files and 256 processes, implemented via an Ansible playbook run from node2 (the node with ansible-core installed, acting as control node). Both node1 and node2 were then each safely restarted one at a time per the mandatory restart protocol, with boot-identity change and post-restart recovery verified.","actions_performed":["Inspected both nodes; found node2 has ansible-core 2.20.5 installed (control node) while node1 does not, so used node2 to orchestrate node1 via Ansible over SSH","Discovered sshd on node1 was inactive/failing (missing host keys and missing /run/sshd privsep dir); ran ssh-keygen -A, created /run/sshd, and enabled/started the ssh service","Wired passwordless SSH from node2 to node1 using the cluster-provided keypair (CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY) via authorized_keys on node1's root account","Wrote an Ansible inventory (node1 target) and a playbook using ansible.builtin.user and ansible.builtin.copy that creates user appworker and writes /etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf with soft/hard nofile=8192 and soft/hard nproc=256","Ran ansible-playbook from node2 against node1; verified successful execution (changed=2 first run)","Verified on node1 via id appworker and su - appworker -c 'ulimit -n; ulimit -u' that the account exists and sessions report nofile=8192 and nproc=256","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, and appworker/limits state on node1; boot_id, uptime -s, and ansible/ssh state on node2","Restarted node1 via backgrounded systemctl reboot so the ack r